  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Regulatory Framework Energy Storage in Ukraine</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project supports the assessment of existing normative framework and the development of comprehensive legal and regulatory changes required for energy development in Ukraine, with focus on battery energy storage systems (BESS).As result of the project, efficient, transparent and non-discriminative regulatory framework on the construction of BESS at the sites of renewable electricity producers, their commissioning and operation at Ukraine&apos;s electricity market is elaborated as part of the process led by the National Energy Regulator (NEURC). Furthermore, when BESS legislation is in place, private investors can construct BESS installations on the sites of renewable power plants, connect them to the grid and operate at the electricity market.Overall, BESS installations will improve efficiency of renewable power plants, reduce curtailment of electricity and improve flexibility of the Ukrainian energy system.The project has a positive impact on:&#x2022;	SDG 7: Affordable and Clean Energy: Ensure access to affordable, reliable, sustainable, and modern energy for all.&#x2022;	SDG 8: Inclusive and sustainable economic growth: support productive activities, decent job creation, entrepreneurship, creativity and innovation.&#x2022;	SDG 9: Promote inclusive and sustainable industrialisation and foster innovation; increase access to finance for small- and medium-sized enterprises (SMEs), upgrade the technological capabilities of industrial sectors.</narrative>
  </description>
